{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>With palms He covers the light</b> — the opposite of <b>behold He spreads His light upon it</b>, as though with palms He covers the light, and the palms are the clouds, like <i>and I will cover you with My palm</i>." "<b>and He commands concerning it</b> — concerning the sun." "<b>in its running</b> [במפגיע] — it is the rain of the clouds, as though it struck the sun, because of the swift course of the clouds."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:45.891967840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}